Negative control for the live playhead (AC3.4 · H4 · design §3.6).

Blinds the line list to the player: every step row is drawn with the mark's
default variant, and the row the player is on carries no `aria-current` and no
accented keyword. The list still renders, one row per parsed step with its line
in the gutter — so what goes red is exactly the claim the line list exists FOR:
a rendered blob and an unmarked list are the same surface, and the reason the
pane parses instead of rendering markdown is the mark.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: scenario-pane.spec.ts — the playhead case (with a playhead set on the
armed track, the row whose `line` matches is the marked one).

FOR THE PROVER: authored by the developer seat from the source line it mutates,
apply-checked with `git apply --check` and reverted; it has NOT been run against
a spec, because the spec is yours and did not exist when this was written. Apply
it blind, confirm the red, then revert.

